              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "VectorEntity.toExcalidraw applies a hand-drawn outline with optional hachure or solid fill. The core implementation uses ExcalidrawModifier, seeded randomness, fill pattern generation and the Excalidraw style manager. Presets coordinate roughness and bowing, while explicit options control color, gap, angle, thickness and line boiling."
        },
        {
          "type": "example",
          "example": "labs/pg-sketchscene"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "seeds-and-line-boiling",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Seeds and line boiling"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabs",
          "tabs": [
            {
              "label": "Boiling",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "example": "labs/pg-sketch-boil"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "An automatic seed derives from entity identity. A fixed numeric seed keeps a specific contour reproducible even when object creation order changes. Scene reset also resets entity sequence numbers. Boiling varies the perturbation over time at a chosen frequency; distinguish its visual cadence from display FPS."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Keep seeds, entity creation order and time sampling stable for offline reproducibility. Randomness driven by Math.random or Date.now in custom updates bypasses those controls."
        }
      ]
    },
